# Locally calculated, and cross-checked byte-for-byte against the copies served
# by Debian (cabextract_1.11.orig.tar.gz) and by the Fedora lookaside cache.
# That agreement is what lets build.sh accept this tarball from a mirror when
# upstream is unreachable -- without a hash file Buildroot takes whatever is
# already sitting in the download directory on faith.
#
# The sha512 line is NOT redundant with the sha256 above it: build.sh builds the
# Fedora lookaside URL out of it, because that cache is addressed by sha512.
# Dropping it silently costs the one mirror here that is never pruned.
